B1 review r2 (Oct 19, 2026), for the main session: /api/feed is not B1's file.

What: when one of /api/feed's engagement sub-reads fails (the count RPC, the
comment rows, or the viewer's own like / repost / save rows), send that field
as null instead of 0 / false. Today a failed read is indistinguishable from
"nobody", and since B1 a feed refresh writes those zeros into the shared
engagement record, over the card's (and the open post's) good values.

Client side is already done in B1's files: seedEngagementFromFeed skips a
null or missing field, and engagementFromFeedPost (the card's fallback before
anything seeds the store) reads null as 0 / false, as before. The only
/api/feed readers are CampusMobile and campus-home, both through those two.
campus-home's FeedPost type still says `like_count: number` etc.; widening it
to `number | null` is optional (nothing reads the raw field outside the store).

Apply with: git apply handoffs/2026-10-19-critique/B1-feed-route-unread-null.patch

